      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dallas firefighter ‘Moe’ Craddock opened a 30‑acre mobile home park in the area, sparking the community that would become Glenn Heights.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenn_Heights%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between 1980 and 1990 the town’s population more than quadrupled, rising from 1,033 to 4,564 residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
